# Example 38: Flow biofilm - rod cells in an LBM microfluidic channel
# (Design 6 Level 2 + Level 3, doc/18-programmable-cell-population-simulation.md §13)
# A colony of rod cells (continuous spherocylinders) grows in a
# pressure-driven channel.  Every tick the D2Q9 lattice-Boltzmann
# solver recomputes the flow around the cells (no-slip bounce-back
# obstacles); the local current then drags the rods downstream
# (Stokes drag) while Hertzian contacts keep them non-overlapping.
# Glucose/O2 advect with the same flow field, so the colony edge sees
# fresh medium while the core turns hypoxic (nutrient boundary layer,
# gate 4).

#promoter name=p_housekeeping strength=-0.4

#gene name=pilT promoter=p_housekeeping
ATG GCT GGT GCT TAA
#end

#media nutrient=GLC concentration=10.0 diffusion_um2_s=300
#media nutrient=O2 concentration=0.25 diffusion_um2_s=20

#config backend=population
#config population_size=64 grid_width=48 grid_height=24
#config cell_shape=rod length_um=4.0 diameter_um=1.0
#config mechanics=contact contact_stiffness=2.0e3
#sim lbm=true relaxation_omega=1.5 lbm_substeps=10
#config dfba=true dfba_dt_h=0.1
#config signaling=true signal_diffusion=0.3 signal_threshold=20.0
#config seed=0
#config ticks=60
#config output=alive_count,diversity_index,core_cell_count,edge_cell_count,core_oxygen_mm,edge_oxygen_mm
